 "sq": [
  {
   "_id": 5211,
   "ANSWER": "<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">In an array-based representation of a binary tree, we map the binary tree to a one-dimensional array. This is done in a level-order fashion, where the root node is placed at index 0, the left child of a node at index i is placed at index 2*i + 1, and the right child of a node at index i is placed at index 2*i + 2.</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">For parent-child relationships:</span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The left child of the node at index i is at index 2*i + 1.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The right child of the node at index i is at index 2*i + 2.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The parent of the node at index i (if i &gt; 0) is at index (i-1) / 2 (integer division).</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Example:</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Consider a binary tree:</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b><img alt=\"A close-up of a triangle\n\nAI-generated content may be incorrect.\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" style=\"width:123px; height:104px\" /></b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">This tree can be represented in an array as: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The root node (1) is at index 0.</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The left child of 1 (2) is at index 1.</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The right child of 1 (3) is at index 2.</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The left child of 2 (4) is at index 3.</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The right child of 2 (5) is at index 4.</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The left child of 3 (6) is at index 5.</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The right child of 3 (7) is at index 6.</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\">&nbsp;</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC201J",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO13",
    "PLO3",
    "PLO2",
    "PLO12"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>What is the representation of a binary tree using an array? Explain how elements are stored in the array.</b></span></span></span></p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 405,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 5211
  },
  {
   "_id": 5212,
   "ANSWER": "<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Advantages:</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Simple and efficient: Array-based binary tree representations are easy to implement, as there is no need for extra pointers or references, unlike in a linked list.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Direct access: We can access any node directly using its index. This makes operations such as searching and accessing nodes very fast.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Cache-friendly: Since the elements are stored in contiguous memory locations, array-based representations are cache-efficient.</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Limitations:</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Fixed size: Once an array is allocated, its size cannot easily be changed. This can be a problem if the tree grows beyond the expected size.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Wasted space: For sparse trees (with many empty child positions), the array may contain a lot of unused slots, wasting memory.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Resizing difficulty: If the tree grows dynamically and the array runs out of space, resizing the array can be inefficient. The whole array might need to be reallocated, which involves copying the existing elements into a new larger array.</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\">&nbsp;</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC201J",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO13",
    "PLO3",
    "PLO2",
    "PLO12"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Describe the advantages and limitations of implementing a binary tree using an array?</b></span></span></span></p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 405,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 5212
  }
 ],
 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 5235,
   "ANSWER": "<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Insertion in Binary Tree (Array Implementation)</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">In a binary tree represented by an array, the parent-child relationships are stored as follows:</span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The root is at index 0.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The left child of a node at index i is at index 2i + 1.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The right child of a node at index i is at index 2i + 2.</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Insertion Operation:</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">To insert a new node in a binary tree represented by an array:</span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The tree should be complete (i.e., every level of the tree is filled except possibly for the last level, which is filled from left to right).</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The new node is inserted at the first available position (next available index in the array).</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Steps for Insertion:</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Find the first empty spot in the array (next available index).</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Insert the node at that position.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The tree maintains its complete property after insertion<b>.</b></span></span></span></span></li>\n</ol>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Example of Insertion:</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">#define MAX 100</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">// Binary Tree representation using an array</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">int tree[MAX];</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">int size = 0;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">// Function to insert a node into the binary tree</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">void insert(int value) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; if (size &lt; MAX) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; tree[size] = value;&nbsp; // Insert the new node</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; size++;&nbsp; // Increment the size to keep track of the next insertion</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; } else {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; printf(&quot;Tree is full\\n&quot;);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; }</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">}</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">// Function to display the tree</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">void display() {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; for (int i = 0; i &lt; size; i++) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; printf(&quot;%d &quot;, tree[i]);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; }</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; printf(&quot;\\n&quot;);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">}</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">int main() {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; insert(10);&nbsp; // Insert root</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; insert(20);&nbsp; // Insert left child</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; insert(30);&nbsp; // Insert right child</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; insert(40);&nbsp; // Insert left child of left child</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; display();&nbsp; // Output the tree: 10 20 30 40</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; return 0;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">}</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Deletion in Binary Tree (Array Implementation)</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Deletion in an array-based binary tree involves removing a node and ensuring the tree&#39;s properties are maintained. Specifically, for deletion:</span></span></span></p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Delete the node.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Replace it with the last node in the array to maintain the completeness of the tree.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Rearrange the tree if necessary.</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ol>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Steps for Deletion:</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Find the node to be deleted (index).</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Replace the node to be deleted with the last node (the node at the last index of the array).</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Decrement the size of the tree to reflect the removal of the node.</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ol>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Example of Deletion:</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">#define MAX 100</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">// Binary Tree representation using an array</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">int tree[MAX];</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">int size = 0;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">// Function to insert a node into the binary tree</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">void insert(int value) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; if (size &lt; MAX) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; tree[size] = value;&nbsp; // Insert the new node</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; size++;&nbsp; // Increment the size to keep track of the next insertion</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; } else {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; printf(&quot;Tree is full\\n&quot;);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; }</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">}</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">// Function to delete a node from the binary tree</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">void deleteNode(int value) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; int i = 0;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Find the node to delete</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; while (i &lt; size &amp;&amp; tree[i] != value) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; i++;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; }</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; if (i == size) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; printf(&quot;Node not found!\\n&quot;);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; return;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; }</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Replace the node with the last node</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; tree[i] = tree[size - 1];</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; size--;&nbsp; // Reduce the size of the tree</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">}</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">// Function to display the tree</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">void display() {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; for (int i = 0; i &lt; size; i++) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; printf(&quot;%d &quot;, tree[i]);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; }</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; printf(&quot;\\n&quot;);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">}</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">int main() {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; insert(10);&nbsp; // Insert root</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; insert(20);&nbsp; // Insert left child</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; insert(30);&nbsp; // Insert right child</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; insert(40);&nbsp; // Insert left child of left child</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; printf(&quot;Tree before deletion: &quot;);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; display();</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; deleteNode(30);&nbsp; // Delete node 30</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; printf(&quot;Tree after deletion: &quot;);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; display();&nbsp; // Output the tree: 10 20 40</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; return 0;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">}</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Tree Maintenance:</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">To maintain the binary tree structure after insertion or deletion, we ensure the following:</span></span></span></p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">After insertion, the tree must remain complete. This can be done by performing a level-order traversal and filling the tree from left to right.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">After deletion, the tree must be balanced. If necessary, re-balance the tree after deleting nodes.</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ol>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif\">Use the correct pointer management to avoid memory leaks and ensure proper linkage between parent and child nodes</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\">&nbsp;</p>\n",
