   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>A company has a hierarchical organizational structure where each employee has a manager, and the structure can be represented as a tree. The CEO is at the root, and each department head manages several employees. The company wants to maintain an efficient system where they can quickly add new employees to specific departments and also handle the removal of employees when they leave the company. The company uses a binary tree to represent this hierarchy.</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Task:</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Insertion: The company wants to add a new employee to a specific department. Explain how you would insert a new employee into the binary tree. What steps will you follow? Write the pseudocode for insertion.</b></span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Deletion: Now, if an employee leaves the company, their record needs to be deleted from the tree. How will you delete a specific employee node from the binary tree? Describe the deletion process and write the pseudocode for it.</b></span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Tree Maintenance: The company needs the hierarchy to be maintained at all times (no broken or invalid connections). Ensure that after insertion or deletion, the structure of the binary tree remains valid and balanced.</b></span></span></span></span></li>\n</ol>\n",
